{
  "mn71:0.1": "Middle Discourses 71 ",
  "mn71:0.2": "To Vacchagotta on the Three Knowledges ",
  "mn71:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn71:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "mn71:2.1": "Now at that time the wanderer Vacchagotta was residing in the Single Lotus monastery for the wanderers. ",
  "mn71:3.1": "Then the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Vesālī for alms. ",
  "mn71:3.2": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "mn71:3.3": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Vesālī. ",
  "mn71:3.4": "Why don’t I visit the wanderer Vacchagotta at the Single Lotus Monastery?” ",
  "mn71:3.5": "So that’s what he did. ",
  "mn71:4.1": "Vacchagotta saw the Buddha coming off in the distance, ",
  "mn71:4.2": "and said to him, ",
  "mn71:4.3": "“Let the Blessed One come, sir! ",
  "mn71:4.4": "Welcome to the Blessed One, sir! ",
  "mn71:4.5": "It’s been a long time since you took the opportunity to come here. ",
  "mn71:4.6": "Please, sir, sit down, here, a seat is ready.” ",
  "mn71:4.7": "The Buddha sat down on the seat spread out, ",
  "mn71:4.8": "while Vacchagotta took a low seat and sat to one side. ",
  "mn71:4.9": "Then Vacchagotta said to the Buddha: ",
  "mn71:5.1": "“Sir, I have heard this: ",
  "mn71:5.2": "‘The ascetic Gotama claims to be all-knowing and all-seeing, to know and see everything without exception, thus: ",
  "mn71:5.3": "“Knowledge and vision are constantly and 